From: GKI maintainers <gki-builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] susfs: mark helpers maybe-unused when the uid filter is off

susfs_switch_to_ksu_domain() and susfs_restore_creds() are unconditional
static definitions in fs/susfs.c, but every call site lives in
susfs_set_priority_uid_filter() and susfs_parse_priority_app_strings(),
which SUSFS compiles only under CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_PRIORITY_UID_FILTER. With
the mount-only profile that symbol is unset, so the definitions have no
callers and -Werror -Wunused-function fails the build. Mark both
definitions __maybe_unused: the attribute is a no-op once the feature is
enabled, and any upstream rename, guard change, or removal of these helpers
fails this patch closed instead of silently diverging.

diff --git a/fs/susfs.c b/fs/susfs.c
--- a/fs/susfs.c
+++ b/fs/susfs.c
@@ -180,5 +180,5 @@
  * susfs_restore_creds() afterwards.
  * Returns the original credentials on success, NULL on failure.
  */
-static struct cred *susfs_switch_to_ksu_domain(void) {
+static struct cred *__maybe_unused susfs_switch_to_ksu_domain(void) {
 	struct cred *orig_cred = NULL;
@@ -214,5 +214,5 @@
  * Restores the original credentials that were saved by
  * susfs_switch_to_ksu_domain().
  */
-static void susfs_restore_creds(struct cred *orig_cred) {
+static void __maybe_unused susfs_restore_creds(struct cred *orig_cred) {
 	if (!orig_cred)
